    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "81447f11_3da5de9b",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/hfpclient/HeadsetClientStateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1966,
      "author": {
        "id": 1979057
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-03T18:35:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi William, after some discussion with @salsavage@google.com and @yuyangh@google.com, we determined it would be preferable to always pass through the disconnecting state. I think it makes stylistic sense to encapsulate all transitions to the disconnected state within disconnecting, which is why we need to check what message brought us to this state because they are processed differently. One reason we want all disconnections, including stack events to pass through the disconnecting state so we can issue the disconnecting broadcast.",
      "parentUuid": "8f6a90a1_653dbdc2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1966,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 1966,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "f352c31c5318c9a810f7095a88a04deaf24fe355",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3566b1de_af954356",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/hfpclient/HeadsetClientStateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1966,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-03T22:56:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But in some case (like when the remote got out of range), there is no \"disconnecting\" to do. I still think this is wrong.\n\n\u003e One reason we want all disconnections, including stack events to pass through the disconnecting state so we can issue the disconnecting broadcast.\n\nThis is phrased like this broadcast was sent prior to this change but it is not. I believe then that nobody listen to the disconnecting and I genuinely wonder if we want to broadcast it at all.\n\nBut I don\u0027t see any issue with broadcasting a transition from CONNECTED to DISCONNECTED if this is was happened with the device. After all, this is what was being done before.",
      "parentUuid": "81447f11_3da5de9b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1966,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 1966,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "f352c31c5318c9a810f7095a88a04deaf24fe355",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9fd0ee5_9e0c4253",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/hfpclient/HeadsetClientStateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1966,
      "author": {
        "id": 1979057
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-23T21:06:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The other half of the profile (AG) utilizes a disconnecting state from the native stack. The state machine is able to rely on the underlying native stack and complete the disconnection. This is the type of behavior we want on the HF side. We want to leverage disconnecting state for clean-up and it is the best place to broadcast disconnecting because most users do not expect a transition from connected to disconnected (there are error warning messages for 2-\u003e0 transitions).  We however don\u0027t have the implementation in native on the HF side, so instead of changing the native code it is easier to insert a disconnecting state as it makes sense for timeouts and passthrough it for clean-up and broadcast and matches user expectations. Code owners would also ideally like for there to be a disconnecting state: https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/btif/src/btif_hf.cc;l\u003d462?q\u003dupstream\u0026sq\u003drepo:android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main%20f:packages%2Fmodules%2FBluetooth",
      "parentUuid": "3566b1de_af954356",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1966,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 1966,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "f352c31c5318c9a810f7095a88a04deaf24fe355",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c0342584_0352d159",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/hfpclient/HeadsetClientStateMachine.java",
