      "writtenOn": "2024-10-03T22:56:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is log as a `WTF` by the statemachine implementation:\n```java\nLog.wtf(mSm.mName, \"transitionTo called while transition already in progress to \" + mDestState + \", new target state\u003d\" + destState);\n```\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/libs/modules-utils/java/com/android/internal/util/StateMachine.java;l\u003d1236;drc\u003d3c7b3fefc7a647aee03bd2b919a70a3dff75ee21\n\nIn this current case, there will be no \"disconnecting\" state since the native call failed, so it doesn\u0027t make sense to me to get into the state in the first place.\nWe should identified what can cause the native call to fail. Maybe we are talking about a case that can not happen and therefor the whole if can be removed ?",
